{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfuL2yqeLLozwtY4yD2qi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I created the dashboard and the alert rule in Kibana, and both exist. The rule is turned on and its first run finished with status `ok`. That means the query runs without errors, but I haven't seen it fire yet.\n\n**1. What the data holds.** `Kibana Sample Data Logs` is time-based on `timestamp`. Each document is one web request, with these main fields:\n- `response`: the HTTP status code, stored as text, with an exact-match `response.keyword` version\n- `bytes`: the size of the response\n- `clientip`: the visitor's IP address\n- `url`, `request` and `referer`: what was asked for and where the visitor came from\n- `extension`: the file type requested\n- `geo.src` and `geo.dest`: source and destination country\n- `machine.os`, `agent` and `tags`: client details\n\n**2. Dashboard: \"EFF-acceb015 Web logs overview\"** (id `eff-acceb015-web-logs-overview-40697b4f2611`). It has 7 panels:\n- Three single numbers: total requests, unique visitors (distinct client IPs) and total bytes served\n- A line chart of requests over time\n- A pie chart of requests by response code\n- A table of the top 10 URLs, with request count and average bytes\n- A bar chart of the top 10 source countries\n\nURL: http://localhost:15601/app/dashboards#/view/eff-acceb015-web-logs-overview-40697b4f2611\n\n**3. Rule: \"EFF-acceb015 5xx spike\"** (id `abec4540-1a7b-4679-87e5-366c085dba03`)\n- It is an Elasticsearch query rule on `kibana_sample_data_logs`, using the `timestamp` field.\n- It runs every minute and fires when more than 10 matching requests arrive within 5 minutes.\n- It finds 5xx responses by looking for `response.keyword` values from \"500\" up to (not including) \"600\". Because the codes are stored as text, they are compared as strings. That gives the right answer only because every status code is three digits.\n- It has no notification action attached, so when it fires the alert only shows up in Kibana. Add a connector, such as email or Slack, if you want to be notified.\n- I added the tag `EFF-acceb015`, which you didn't ask for."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":666,"cache_read_input_tokens":21318,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":666},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0536cbf5-c97a-5467-80bd-e50c5d30a2ce","uuid":"a8a0411c-f18e-4b3b-9e47-abccd3c05dc2","timestamp":"2026-10-10T22:16:03.298Z","request_id":"req_011CfuL2ydjZHAYSwAgdakcJ"}
